# ============================================================
# pi-swarm Configuration
# ============================================================
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your values:
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# The provider/model pair below is the recommended Codex subscription setup.
# It selects the same practical default used in TUTORIAL.md.
# Authenticate with pi's /login (ChatGPT Plus/Pro (Codex)); do not add an API key.
# The provider you choose here will be used for all agent tiers
# (orchestrator, team leads, and workers) by default.
# You can override per-tier in code if needed.
# ============================================================

# --- Recommended: pi subscription / OAuth ---
PROVIDER=openai-codex
MODEL=gpt-5.6-luna

# `/login` authenticates the Codex subscription. This is different from
# `PROVIDER=openai`, which sends requests through the OpenAI API and requires
# an API key with API billing.

# ============================================================
# API Keys — Uncomment the one matching your PROVIDER above
# ============================================================

# --- Google Gemini ---
# Get your key at: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# GEMINI_API_KEY=your-gemini-api-key-here

# --- OpenAI ---
# Get your key at: https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
# For API-key mode, set PROVIDER=openai and MODEL=gpt-5.6-luna above.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-your-openai-key-here

# --- Anthropic ---
# Get your key at: https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-your-anthropic-key-here

# --- Groq ---
# Get your key at: https://console.groq.com/keys
# GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_your-groq-key-here

# --- OpenRouter (access many models with one key) ---
# Get your key at: https://openrouter.ai/keys
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-your-openrouter-key-here

# --- Mistral ---
# Get your key at: https://console.mistral.ai/api-keys
# MISTRAL_API_KEY=your-mistral-key-here

# --- xAI (Grok) ---
# Get your key at: https://console.x.ai
# XAI_API_KEY=your-xai-key-here
